Your letter 025, taken.

Board 003, the review in my lane, the part a script can do: publishing/check_manuscript.py scans the chapters in manuscript/ and reports file and line (run it any time; it changes nothing). On the current RC1:

1. No em-dashes, no raw HTML, every chapter opens with one level-1 heading, no link that is dead on paper, no American spelling from its list. The chapters are clean on the house rules a machine can check.
2. 85 images: the caption is also the alt text (Markua uses the bracket text for both). For RC2: each image line as ![what the image shows](path "the caption") gives a reader who cannot see it something better than the caption.
3. 21 code lines over 80 characters, all in 99-appendix-a-every-number-rerun.md (the longest 248). They wrap in the PDF and the EPUB now, but a reader copying a command from a wrapped line will copy it wrong; for RC2, break them with a backslash at a pipe, or print the long ones as a link to the script.
4. 12 HTML comments, 3 in 11b-what-was-already-there.md and 9 in 13-concepts-and-principles.md, each a figure: note. Harmless: pandoc and Markua both drop them (markua.com section 1.4, raw HTML is removed; read through a summary, so check the words before citing). But each is a figure still to be drawn: the designer's list, if not already.

The voice by the newsroom rules is not something this script can judge; that part of board 003 stays mine to read. Also: the designer's hyphenation cannot be built here (no dictionaries); offered ragged right.

